# Taxonomy

The canonical vocabulary of the project. One row per term, one physical line per row. Bold appears only in the Term column.

## Product

| Term | Means | Not | Lives in |
|---|---|---|---|
| **proxy token** | A random value with the prefix `lpt_` that lets a client use the proxy; the binary stores only its SHA-256 hash, with a unique name and key=value tags. | A provider credential that the agent sends to the upstream; a GitHub token label. | `docs/specification/tokens.md` |
| **provider account** | The identity of the account at the model provider, stored only as an HMAC-SHA256 of a stable account ID or of the credential, with `LOUPE_ACCOUNT_KEY`. | A proxy token, which identifies the client of the proxy, not the provider account. | `docs/specification/accounts.md` |
| **exchange** | One request and its response that the proxy forwards and stores, with encrypted bodies and redacted credentials. | A call, which the parser finds inside an exchange. | `docs/specification/proxy.md` |
| **call** | One model call that the parser finds from the usage block in the response of an exchange, with its token counts and cost. | An exchange, which is the raw stored request and response. | `docs/specification/parser-sessions.md` |
| **session** | A group of calls of one agent and one proxy token that closes after `LOUPE_IDLE_SECS` with no calls; a subagent is its own session. | A segment, which is the part of a session on one day; a day record. | `docs/specification/parser-sessions.md` |
| **segment** | The part of a session that falls on one day, so a session that spans midnight counts on each day that has a call. | A session, which can span more than one day. | `docs/specification/parser-sessions.md` |
| **day record** | The published totals of one day in `LOUPE_TZ`: tokens, calls, sessions, cost, unpriced calls, pull requests, lines, and a summary. | A session; a day with no calls and no GitHub activity, which has no record. | `docs/specification/days-public-api.md` |
| **upstream** | A named provider base URL in `upstreams.toml` that the proxy can forward to; the file is also the allowlist of hosts. | An agent label, which names the client, not the destination. | `docs/specification/proxy.md` |
| **agent label** | The name of the agent in the proxy route, for example `claude-code` or `pi`, from `/<agent>/<upstream>/<path>`. | An upstream, which names the provider. | `docs/specification/proxy.md` |
| **API-equivalent cost** | The cost of a call at the list price of the provider API from the vendored LiteLLM price file, also when the agent uses a subscription. | The price that the user paid for a subscription. | `docs/specification/cost.md` |
| **unpriced call** | A call with no matching price entry or a missing price field for a non-zero token count; its cost is null and it counts in `unpriced_calls`. | A call with a cost of zero. | `docs/specification/cost.md` |
| **GitHub token label** | The `<LABEL>` part of a `LOUPE_GITHUB_TOKEN_<LABEL>` variable, recorded with each pull request so an analysis can group by it. | A proxy token; the GitHub token value, which stays in the environment. | `docs/specification/github.md` |
| **public API** | The open-CORS routes `GET /v1/days`, `GET /v1/days/{day}`, and `GET /healthz` that other sites can read. | The dashboard, which is a page that reads the public API. | `docs/specification/days-public-api.md` |
| **dashboard** | The page that the same binary serves at `GET /`, which reads `/v1/days` and shows the data. | The public API, which returns data and no page. | `docs/specification/dashboard.md` |

## Foundation

| Term | Means | Not | Lives in |
|---|---|---|---|
| **configuration source** | Where the loader got an effective value: one of `flag`, `env`, `file`, or `default`, in that order of precedence. | The file for the environment `config/<env>.toml`, which is one source only. | `docs/specification/configuration.md` |
| **pipeline entry point** | A script under `.agents/scripts/` that does one stage of the pipeline, for example `pipeline.test.sh`. | A platform thin caller, which only calls an entry point. | `.agents/scripts/`, `docs/specification/operations.md` |
| **verdict** | The result of `pipeline.verdict.sh`: one `status: passed` or `status: failed` line per stage, the times, and an exit code. | The result of one stage entry point alone. | `.agents/scripts/pipeline.verdict.sh`, `docs/specification/operations.md` |
